@startuml
title P1 Presence, DND and Block State

hide empty description

state "Presence generation" as Presence {
  [*] --> online : authenticated message <= 12 s
  online --> offline : heartbeat stale > 12 s
  offline --> online : current binding authenticates
  online : output ready/degraded
  online : playback idle/main/overlay/interrupt/unknown
  offline : output unavailable
  offline : playback unknown
  offline : interrupt-resume false
}

state "Layered DND" as DND {
  [*] --> allow_all
  allow_all --> messages_only : expected revision + 1
  allow_all --> muted_until : expected revision + 1
  messages_only --> allow_all : owner mutation
  messages_only --> muted_until : stricter layer
  muted_until --> allow_all : coordinator deadline expires
  muted_until --> messages_only : owner mutation
}

state "Recipient block" as Block {
  [*] --> active : viewer-scoped ar_/or_ ref
  active --> revoked : owner delete
  revoked --> [*] : never resurrect queued work
}

DND --> missed_dnd : non-started suppression
DND --> cancelled_dnd : active fade-stop
Block --> blocked : pre-play actor/orbit block
Block --> sender_blocked : active fade-stop

note bottom
  Effective DND is the stricter local/orbit layer. Remote orbit state
  cannot loosen local state. Exact retries are actor-scoped and durable.
  Presence never exposes actor ids, credentials, device/process names,
  microphone/capture state, levels, paths, addresses or media URLs.
end note

@enduml
